# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Morrow Coffee Co. — ignored paths
#
# Ignoring a path only affects files that are *not already tracked*. If
# something here is already in the repo, `git rm --cached <path>` it once.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local.html

# Test artefacts
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/
.vitest/

# Environment — never commit real values
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Misc
.cache/
.temp/
tmp/

# TypeScript incremental build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large media
#
# Source masters are large and are not needed to build or run the site — the
# optimised files in `public/media/` are what ships. Keeping masters out of Git
# keeps clones and deploys small; `assets/source/` is the documented home for a
# master when one genuinely must be versioned (see docs/VIDEO_SETUP.md).
#
# Raw camera/export dumps and phone recordings:
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.wmv
*.flv
*.m4v
*.psd
*.ai
*.indd

# ...except anything deliberately banked as a source master:
!assets/source/*.mov
!assets/source/*.mp4

# Phone-sync junk that shows up when uploading from iOS
IMG_[0-9]*.HEIC
IMG_[0-9]*.heic
*.HEIC
*.heic

# A heavily-compressed duplicate of a delivered file is almost always an
# accident; the encode ladder in public/media/ is the reviewed set.
public/images/*.mp4
public/images/*.webm
